+/* Which file a Claude Code hook lands in decides which SESSIONS run it — and this hook's
+ * command is principal-scoped, so the file decides whose directed mail a session surfaces.
+ * From the Claude Code docs (code.claude.com/docs/en/settings, "Settings files and who they
+ * affect"; docs/en/hooks names the same three files as hook sources):
+ *
+ *   ~/.claude/settings.json       user            "You, in every project on this machine"
+ *   .claude/settings.json         shared project  "Everyone working in the folder that contains it"
+ *   .claude/settings.local.json   project local   "You, in this one project only"
+ *
+ * The default used to be the user file. Installing agent A and then agent B there left only
+ * B's command, and every session of this OS user — A's included — then surfaced B's mail: the
+ * shared-host leak 0.1.40 closed, reopened (Codex exact review, 2026-09-01). The binding has
+ * to be session-local, so the default is now the project-local file and --user is explicit
+ * and loud.
+ *
+ * Placement follows the same page ("Where Claude Code keeps the local file in a git
+ * repository"): inside a repository the local file is read at the repository root — from a
+ * linked worktree, at the MAIN checkout's root — and it stays beside .claude/settings.json in
+ * the working directory outside a repository or when the repository root is the home
+ * directory. Claude Code adds a global git exclude for the local file only when IT creates
+ * the file; one we create is ours to keep out of git, so a non-ignored path is refused with
+ * the exact .gitignore line, as --repo has always done.
+ *
+ * CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR (docs/en/env-vars): "Override the configuration directory (default:
+ * ~/.claude). All settings, session history, and plugins are stored under this path." */
+type ClaudeHookScope = "project-local" | "repo" | "user";
+
+const CLAUDE_REPO_SETTINGS_FILE = ".claude/settings.json";
+const CLAUDE_LOCAL_SETTINGS_FILE = ".claude/settings.local.json";
+
+function claudeConfigDirectory(): string {
+  const configured = process.env.CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR;
+  if (configured === undefined || configured.trim() === "") return join(homedir(), ".claude");
+  return isAbsolute(configured) ? configured : join(process.cwd(), configured);
+}
 
